A||||6||cowans||Muncie 4 sp > Isuzu 5 sp???||||1||
Z||000000||cowans||12-13-2001||12:52 PM||||I have been running a 4 sp to a V8 and am presently building up a new V8(300+). I have not been impressed with the 4sp and would like to possibly install Isuzu 5sp (as Getrags are  "Gold" up here.) As I understand it, I need a 5sp stick and cables and mounts from the Isuzu. Can I use the Centerforce & T.O. bearing from my 4 sp??? Are the axles (4sp/5sp) the same?? Anything else???<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroPerformance||12-13-2001||02:52 PM||||You need the throw out bearing that matches the tranny. As for the clutch and pressure plate, I think you can use the Getrag setup. I am about to try that on mine because my 4 cylinder clutch is slipping.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||12-13-2001||03:18 PM||||The axles are interchangable.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||12-13-2001||04:05 PM||||You need everything that goes with the trans.  When I did my isuzu 5 speed install I needed the shifter, cables, trans and clutch assembly for the Isuzu 5 speed.  Might need a new slave cylinder too.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000004||tesmith66||12-13-2001||05:09 PM||||CLutch and pressure plate from 4 speed or Getrag (interchangeable) and T/O bearing from Isuzu. Slave cylinders on 4 speed and Isuzu interchange. Getrag has different slave.<P>You also need the 5 speed shifter and cables. You also have to tie the cables away from the throttle cable at the throttle body.<P>I have this setup on my 86 SE V6. Works great. Email me if you want some pics.<P>Also, chech my reply here: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015486.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015486.html</A> <BR>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe<p>[This message has been edited by tesmith66 (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||cowans||12-14-2001||07:43 AM||||Thanks to all who answered! All my questions answered.<BR>Merry Christmas!||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPAW||12-14-2001||12:56 PM||||If you are putting the transmission in an 84 you will need the plug from the wiring harness of the donor car so you can wire up the backup lights. 4spd backup switch on shifter, 5 speed on transmission.  85 and up may already have the plug on the wiring harness.<P>I am in the process of doing the same swap - couldn't stand the screaming high revs at cruise speed with the 4.11, 4spd.<P>Drop me an email we can trade notes - MrPAW@aol.com.||||reg||1
